#### Description

Verified with [dockhand](https://github.com/herbygillot/dockhand):
  — libwidget on Tahoe: linted clean, built in a pristine VM.
  — gegl on Tahoe: linted clean, built in a pristine VM.
  — gegl-devel on Tahoe: the build failed — it was to be built with gegl deactivated, at the maintainer's request — and this was promoted anyway.

ABI changed: install name /opt/local/lib/libwidget.2.dylib → /opt/local/lib/libwidget.3.dylib; libwidget compatibility_version 2.0.0 → 3.0.0 (narrowed), measured between libwidget@2.4.1 (binary archive) and @3.0 (built from source) on Testos.
this criterion is necessary and not sufficient: an install name and a compatibility version can sit still while symbols are removed, and a break confined to a header or to a plugin's own contract is invisible to otool.

Revision bumped in this change:
  — gegl (graphics/gegl): depends_lib; /opt/local/bin/gegl links against /opt/local/lib/libwidget.3.dylib
  — gegl-devel (graphics/gegl-devel): depends_lib; conflicts with gegl, which this cohort builds — forced into the build at the maintainer's request, with gegl deactivated first; the build failed, so nothing was measured

Branch head `0123456789ab`.

